{
  "about": "The solar-verify that exports a loop function's spec (tools/certify/loop_final.py spec_exporter): an immutable copy of O6's binary, checked by SHA-256; the shared checkout's solar-verify lacks O6's spec-scope fixes (review 189). Built with cargo build --locked -p solar-verify --bin solar-verify (debug, local, SHIPPY_REMOTE unset) in the tree at the commit, cargo reporting it fresh, then copied read-only to binary (relative to the repository root, or CERTIFY_SPEC_VERIFY_BINARY; tree likewise, or CERTIFY_SPEC_VERIFY_TREE). Debug builds are not reproducible across machines and caches, so nothing rebuilds it at run time. The pinned commit also writes the loop heads of every function past a failing spec (abca4e4c5: --emit-loop-heads exits 0 and records each failing function's status and failures), which tools/certify/loop_cuts.py's heads_exporter runs.",
